    "answer": {
      "short": "$y=\\frac{1}{8}$",
      "worked": "Since $y$ varies inversely with the cube of $x$,\n$$y=\\frac{k}{x^3}.$$\nUsing $x=2$ and $y=1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}1&=\\frac{k}{2^3}\\\\k&=8\\end{align*}$$\nWhen $x=4$:\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\frac{8}{4^3}\\\\y&=\\frac{1}{8}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
